blocklist (formerly blacklist) from https://github.com/zoulasc/blocklist

Vendor branch: vendor/blocklist, tagged vendor/blocklist/YYYYMMDD after
the upstream commit date.  Upstream has no releases; import HEAD.

To import a new snapshot:

  1) git clone https://github.com/zoulasc/blocklist.git and note the
     commit hash and date.
  2) In this repository:
	git fetch <clone> HEAD
	c=$(git commit-tree FETCH_HEAD^{tree} -p vendor/blocklist \
	    -m "Import blocklist YYYY-MM-DD (shorthash)")
	git branch -f vendor/blocklist $c
	git tag vendor/blocklist/YYYYMMDD $c
  3) On master:
	git merge -X subtree=contrib/blocklist vendor/blocklist
  4) Re-run sh midnightbsd-changes.sh in contrib/blocklist and check
     that nothing else changed with
	git diff vendor/blocklist HEAD:contrib/blocklist
  5) If source files were added or removed, update lib/libblocklist,
     usr.sbin/blocklistd and usr.sbin/blocklistctl.
  6) Build world and test sshd(8) and fingerd(8) integration.

Files that are not upstream:

  bin/blacklistctl.c bin/blacklistd.c bin/old_internal.[ch]
  include/blacklist.h include/old_bl.h lib/blacklist.c lib/old_bl.c
  bin/blacklistctl.8 bin/blacklistd.8 bin/blacklistd.conf.5 lib/libblacklist.3
	Compatibility sources for the old blacklist names, taken from
	FreeBSD.  They build lib/libblacklist, usr.sbin/blacklistd and
	usr.sbin/blacklistctl so existing configurations keep working
	with a warning.
  port/config.h
	Wrapper that pulls in port/port.h; upstream generates this with
	autoconf.
  midnightbsd-changes.sh MIDNIGHTBSD-upgrade
	This file and the change script.
